window.docContents[168].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Drivers.Random/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Drivers___Random":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Drivers › Random.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 28 of 56 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nEntropy SyscallsDefines the Linux AArch64 getrandom syscall number (SYS_GETRANDOM = 278), GRND_* flag constants (include/uapi/linux/random.h), and handler execGetrandom (drivers/char/random.c).\n\n\n\ndef SYS_GETRANDOML25–26 ↗#Linux AArch64 getrandom syscall number (__NR_getrandom = 278, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:762, drivers/char/random.c:1395).\n\ndef GRND_NONBLOCKL28–29 ↗#Linux getrandom flags (include/uapi/linux/random.h:47-49).\n\ndef GRND_RANDOML30 ↗#\n\ndef GRND_INSECUREL31 ↗#\n\ndef GRND_KNOWN_MASKL32 ↗#\n\ndef execGetrandomL34–57 ↗#getrandom(buf, count, flags) (__NR_getrandom = 278, drivers/char/random.c:1395):* flags is unsigned int (W2): rejects bits outside GRND_KNOWN_MASK (0x7) and the mutually exclusive combination GRND_INSECURE | GRND_RANDOM (0x6) with -EINVAL.* count > MAX_RW_COUNT (0x7ffff000) returns -EINVAL without writing memory or advancing oracleIdx (Linux clamps count to MAX_RW_COUNT for a short read).* Assumes an initialized kernel CRNG, so GRND_NONBLOCK never returns -EAGAIN and valid requests fill count bytes from s.oracle.getrandom s.oracleIdx.* Checks flags before checking s.mem.canWrite buf count.toNat (copy_to_user).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Drivers/Random.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Drivers.Random/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Drivers___Random"},"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.ReadWrite/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___ReadWrite":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs › ReadWrite.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 216 of 255 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (13)def SYS_LSEEKdef SYS_READdef SYS_WRITEdef SYS_PREAD64def FsState.fileBytesdef FsState.writePosdef writeFileBytesdef FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZEdef execReadCommondef execReaddef execWritedef execLseekdef execPread64\n\nLinux VFS Read, Write, and Seek SyscallsTrusted Computing Base model of Linux lseek (__NR_lseek = 62), read (__NR_read = 63), write (__NR_write = 64), and pread64 (__NR_pread64 = 67) over FsState (fs/read_write.c in Linux 7.3).\n\n\n\ndef SYS_LSEEKL26–27 ↗#Linux AArch64 lseek syscall number (__NR_lseek = 62, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:204, fs/read_write.c:324).\n\ndef SYS_READL29–30 ↗#Linux AArch64 read syscall number (__NR_read = 63, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:206, fs/read_write.c:709).\n\ndef SYS_WRITEL32–33 ↗#Linux AArch64 write syscall number (__NR_write = 64, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:208, fs/read_write.c:733).\n\ndef SYS_PREAD64L35–36 ↗#Linux AArch64 pread64 syscall number (__NR_pread64 = 67, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:214, fs/read_write.c:756).\n\ndef FsState.fileBytesL38–42 ↗#Current byte contents of regular file path in fs ([] if absent or a directory).\n\ndef FsState.writePosL44–47 ↗#Effective starting byte offset for write on desc in fs ((fs.fileBytes desc.path).length when O_APPEND is set, otherwise desc.offset; fs/read_write.c:1735 generic_write_checks).\n\ndef writeFileBytesL49–53 ↗#Overwrite or extend old starting at byte offset pos with src, zero-padding any gap (fs/read_write.c:588 vfs_write).\n\ndef FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZEL55–62 ↗#Conservative cross-filesystem regular-file offset/size bound (0xffffffff = 4,294,967,295 bytes, 4 GiB - 1): lies at or below s_maxbytes across tmpfs (MAX_LFS_FILESIZE = 2 ^ 63 - 1), 1 KiB/2 KiB/4 KiB-block and non-extent ext4 (≥ ~2 TiB, fs/ext4/super.c ext4_max_size), and vfat (4 GiB - 1). Failing closed at newOff ≥ FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZE on lseek (note vfs_setpos checks offset > maxsize, so failing closed at ≥ is sound) and pos + count.toNat > FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZE on write keeps the model sound across common host filesystems.\n\ndef execReadCommonL64–120 ↗#Cooperative full-slice read (__NR_read = 63, fs/read_write.c:709 ksys_read) and pread64 (__NR_pread64 = 67, fs/read_write.c:756 ksys_pread64):* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: Models complete reads clamped to MAX_RW_COUNT = 0x7ffff000 (count' := min count.toNat MAX_RW_COUNT, fs/read_write.c:568-569 vfs_read) on .localFile descriptors (with rw_verify_area returning -EINVAL when pos + count.toNat > MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, matching fs/read_write.c:458-472, 565-567), sequential .stdio stdin (fd = 0, useExplicitPos = false), and read (!useExplicitPos) on .localDir descriptors (-EISDIR, fs/libfs.c:223 generic_read_dir, assuming getdents/getdents64 is unmodeled so directory f_pos remains 0); fails closed with .Exception when chunk faults after a writable prefix (canWrite buf 1 && !canWrite buf chunk.length), or on pread64 (useExplicitPos = true) on .localDir, closed fd < 3, or other non-file FDs.* [OVERPINNED_BEHAVIOR]: Checks posR < 0 (-EINVAL) before fd on pread64 (fs/read_write.c:756-761), checks accMode.canRead (FMODE_READ) and access_ok (buf.toNat + count.toNat > USER_VA_LIMIT -> -EFAULT) before rw_verify_area (pos + count.toNat > MAX_LFS_FILESIZE -> -EINVAL) and the MAX_RW_COUNT clamp, and checks user buffer writability only on the chunk.length bytes actually copied (mm/filemap.c copy_page_to_iter, so chunk.length = 0 at EOF returns 0 without faulting).\n\ndef execReadL122–124 ↗#read(fd, buf, count) (__NR_read = 63, fs/read_write.c:709 SYSCALL_DEFINE3(read)).\n\ndef execWriteL126–202 ↗#write(fd, buf, count) (__NR_write = 64, fs/read_write.c:733 SYSCALL_DEFINE3(write)): stream trace output for fd ∈ {1, 2}; file update otherwise.* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: Models complete writes clamped to MAX_RW_COUNT = 0x7ffff000 (count' := min count.toNat MAX_RW_COUNT, fs/read_write.c:681-682 vfs_write) on stdout/stderr (fd ∈ {1, 2}) and open .localFile descriptors (returning -EINVAL when count > 0 and desc.offset + count.toNat > MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, matching fs/read_write.c:458-472 rw_verify_area on file->f_pos), and returns -EBADF on .localDir descriptors; fails closed with .Exception when buf faults after a readable prefix (allPerm (·.r) buf 1 && !allPerm (·.r) buf count'), when a file write exceeds FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZE (0xffffffff) or MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, or on closed fd = 0 or custom FDs.* [OVERPINNED_BEHAVIOR]: Checks fd, accMode.canWrite (FMODE_WRITE), access_ok (buf.toNat + count.toNat > USER_VA_LIMIT -> -EFAULT, including count = 0), count == 0 (0), and rw_verify_area (desc.offset + count.toNat > MAX_LFS_FILESIZE -> -EINVAL) on the unclamped count before clamping to MAX_RW_COUNT and reading buf, returning -EFAULT only when the first byte is not readable (!allPerm (·.r) buf 1, matching mm/filemap.c generic_perform_write).\n\ndef execLseekL204–249 ↗#lseek(fd, offset, whence) (__NR_lseek = 62, fs/read_write.c:412 SYSCALL_DEFINE3(lseek) -> ksys_lseek -> generic_file_llseek_size, include/uapi/linux/fs.h:52-57 SEEK_SET = 0, SEEK_CUR = 1, SEEK_END = 2, SEEK_DATA = 3, SEEK_HOLE = 4):* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: Models SEEK_SET/SEEK_CUR/SEEK_END below FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZE (0xffffffff) and past-EOF SEEK_DATA/SEEK_HOLE (offS ≥ fileLen -> -ENXIO, matching fs/read_write.c:122-138, mm/shmem.c:3606, and fs/ext4/file.c) on .localFile descriptors; fails closed with .Exception on newOff ≥ FS_SAFE_MAX_FILESIZE, negative or in-bounds SEEK_DATA/SEEK_HOLE (offS < fileLen), non-seekable .stdio (fd < 3), and .localDir descriptors.\n\ndef execPread64L251–256 ↗#pread64(fd, buf, count, pos) (__NR_pread64 = 67, fs/read_write.c:756 SYSCALL_DEFINE4(pread64)).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs/ReadWrite.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.ReadWrite/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___ReadWrite"}});